// Project-level base configuration, wired in by project.yml's `configFiles`.
// Its only job is to pull in the developer's personal signing settings.
//
// `#include?` is xcconfig's optional include: if signing.local.xcconfig does
// not exist (CI, fresh clone), the line is silently skipped and no team is
// set — simulator and macOS builds need none. To build to a physical device,
// create signing.local.xcconfig (git-ignored) next to this file containing:
//
//   DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = <your team ID>
//
// Leave it unscoped: an [sdk=...]-conditional team breaks
// -allowProvisioningUpdates' App Group registration for the widget, the same
// failure mode as a command-line DEVELOPMENT_TEAM= override (see CLAUDE.md).
// On a free Personal Team the unscoped value makes a *signed* macOS build
// impossible (no macOS App Groups there) — build macOS with
// CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO, exactly as CI does.
//
// Automatic signing does the rest: certificate, App IDs, App Groups, profiles.
#include? "signing.local.xcconfig"
